      "writtenOn": "2024-07-19T19:52:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there any reason that we can\u0027t just copy the uniform data to a global, instead of putting it on the stack and then passing it around across all the functions?\n\nPassing a function parameter around is technically a copy that we are hoping the compiler might optimize away, but there\u0027s a real risk that the compiler fails to eliminate the copy. Using a global eliminates that risk.\n\nIf this were Metal or something we could pass a reference but GLSL is purely pass-by-copy.",
      "revId": "1d4f775b097ff1e19e1b8ee350443365c67bde7e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
