      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-19T19:58:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will test the performance with holding the struct as a global. It does have a lot of simplicity to it, although I am averse to global variables (although the reason for that are unfounded, so...) In practice, most of these function calls are inlined away entirely at the sksl level, but I had been thinking about having the MSL generator use references to ensure we don\u0027t have a copy.\n\nI am not concerned about GLSL in this case because if/when Graphite emits glsl it will not be using storage buffers to aggregate uniform data so will not trigger this specific mode.",
